@@ -54,6 +58,10 @@ The element processes metadata through the custom library to generate message pa
 
     The actual message format depends entirely on the implementation of your custom library. The above is just an example from the provided default library. For detailed implementation guidance and complete JSON structure examples, refer to **Chapter 4. Writing Your Own Application**.
 
+    `sensorId`, `nodeId`, `ptsNs` and `captureTime` are omitted when unset. `captureTime` is the UTC capture time (RFC 3339) taken from the buffer's `timestamp/x-unix` or `timestamp/x-ntp` reference (for `rtspsrc`, enable `add-reference-timestamp-meta`); other references are ignored.
+
+    With `payload-type=protobuf` the default library emits `dxstream.SensorFrame` (`dx_msgconvl/proto/dx_frame.proto`) with the same fields; `capture_time` is a `google.protobuf.Timestamp`.
+
     In the default library, frame-level segmentation remains a full-frame semantic class map, while object-level `segment` payloads are ROI-local binary masks aligned to the corresponding `object.box`.
 
 ### **Hierarchy**
@@ -94,6 +102,10 @@ Custom message-converter libraries must follow the error reporting contract desc
 | `library-file-path` | Path to the custom message converter library. **Required**.       | String    | `null`           |
 | `message-interval` | Frame interval at which message is converted.                      | Integer    | `1`             |
 | `include-frame`  | Flag whether to include frame data as base64 JPEG in the message. (optional). | Boolean   | `false`          |
+| `node-id`        | Identifier of this node, emitted in each message. (optional). | String | `null` |
+| `payload-type`   | Serialization format the custom library should emit: `json` or `protobuf`. The protobuf backend of the default library is built only when libprotobuf and protoc are found. | Enum | `json` |
+
+Each message also carries a broker key: the source's `sensor-id` (see **DxInputSelector**), or none if unset. **DxMsgBroker** with Kafka sends it as the message key, so one source's messages stay in order on one partition.
 
